From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rework LinkedIn post flow: human-sounding copy + automatic
 Polaris tag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The share page shipped one AI-flavoured caption (rocket/sparkle emoji, an
emoji bullet row, generic sensory filler) that all 30 students would post
verbatim. Near-identical posts get suppressed, and the "don't forget to
tag Polaris" line in the subtitle left the actual tagging to chance.

Post data
- Four caption angles (the moment / what changed / the shout-out / why I
  came) instead of one. Thirty different posts travel; thirty copies of
  the same post do not.
- Rewrote all copy in plain first-person: no emoji, short declaratives,
  a hook under 120 chars, one question at the end to pull comments, and
  three hashtags rather than a decorated block.
- Two personalisation fields (one real detail, someone to thank) feed
  into the template, so no two students post the same words.

Automatic Polaris tagging
- Every angle places "@Polaris School of Technology" inside the first two
  paragraphs, so it lands above LinkedIn's ~210-char fold.
- ensureMention() re-inserts the tag above the hashtag block if a student
  edits it out; it runs on both share and copy, so the caption that leaves
  the page always carries the tag.
- A live status line shows whether the tag is present, with one tap to
  restore it.
- Step 6 explains how to convert the pasted text into a real mention
  (retype @Polaris, pick the page from the dropdown) since pasted text
  alone does not notify the page. Includes a copy-the-page-name button.

UX
- Numbered steps, a "save photo" button, and a sticky action bar.
- Live LinkedIn feed preview showing exactly what shows before
  "…see more", with the mention rendered as it will appear.
- Character and hook counters, plus a warning when the tag falls behind
  the fold or the first line runs long.
- Drafts persist in localStorage; switching angles over hand-written text
  offers an undo.
- Clipboard fallback for non-secure contexts, AbortError no longer treated
  as a share failure, aria-live status, and a reduced-motion media query.
- Collapsible reach tips (timing, no outbound links, reply in hour one).

The base64 photo is untouched, byte for byte.

